WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:06.295
Let's build this haunted backyard in the
Scene Builder. A fenced graveyard, a crypt,

00:00:06.295 --> 00:00:09.388
glowing lanterns, and
skeletons that actually move.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.765
We'll start from an empty plot, and
build it step by step. It's free,

00:00:13.765 --> 00:00:15.719
and it runs right in your browser.

00:00:16.233 --> 00:00:21.627
Step one. Click New project. Give it a
name, keep Empty plot and Day lighting,

00:00:21.627 --> 00:00:27.159
and create it. Daylight is easier to build
in. We'll switch to night at the end.

00:00:27.533 --> 00:00:31.842
With nothing selected, the panel on
the right shows the scene settings.

00:00:31.842 --> 00:00:34.877
Change the ground to Dark,
and make it 160 m wide.

00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:39.808
Step two, the floor. The Halloween
kit is already open on the left.

00:00:39.808 --> 00:00:43.700
Set the grid step to 4 m. These
floor tiles are 4 m wide,

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.499
so now they will snap together perfectly.

00:00:46.867 --> 00:00:50.609
Pick Floor Dirt, and click in the scene
to drop the first tile in the far corner.

00:00:50.967 --> 00:00:56.735
It flickers, because its top is
level with the ground. Press Esc,

00:00:56.735 --> 00:01:02.326
and lower the ground level to
−0.5. Now the floor stands clear.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.467
The tile is selected, so the
inspector shows its settings.

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:13.779
Scroll down to the Array tool, and ask for
9 copies, 4 m apart. That's one full row.

00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:17.808
Press Ctrl+A to select the whole
row, Ctrl+D to duplicate it,

00:01:17.808 --> 00:01:22.809
then nudge the copy into place with the
arrow keys. Repeat until the floor is done.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.616
For the open grave, click
one tile, delete it,

00:01:27.616 --> 00:01:30.258
and drop a Floor Dirt Grave in the gap.

00:01:30.633 --> 00:01:34.633
It lands on the lowered ground,
so set its Y position back to 0.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:40.250
Press Ctrl+A, then L, to lock the floor,
so you can't move it by accident.

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:48.379
Step three, the fence. Set the
grid step to 2 m. Pick Fence,

00:01:48.379 --> 00:01:53.530
drop one piece on the back edge,
and array it. 7 copies, 4 m apart.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.504
For the sides, pick the fence again,

00:01:56.504 --> 00:02:01.061
and press Shift + ] to turn it
90° before you click. This time,

00:02:01.061 --> 00:02:03.231
array it along Z instead of X.

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:08.777
Do the same on the other
side and along the front,

00:02:08.777 --> 00:02:11.209
leaving a gap in the
middle for the Arch Gate.

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:17.182
Then put a Fence Pillar on every
joint. Hold Shift while you click,

00:02:17.182 --> 00:02:19.068
and the part stays in your hand.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.991
Swap a few pieces for the broken
versions, so it all looks old.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:31.696
Step four. Set the grid step
to 0.5 m for finer work,

00:02:31.696 --> 00:02:36.578
and lay a path from the gate towards
the back. There are four path pieces,

00:02:36.578 --> 00:02:37.567
so mix them up.

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:43.240
To find any part quickly, just
search for it. Type crypt,

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.434
and place it at the end of the path.

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:48.785
Then add skull candles and
candle clusters by its door.

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:55.350
Step five, the graves. Place them in
two blocks, either side of the path.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:58.787
Hold Shift to stamp a few, then
switch to another headstone,

00:02:58.787 --> 00:03:00.449
so no two rows look the same.

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:07.015
Add a coffin by the open
grave, another near the crypt,

00:03:07.015 --> 00:03:09.942
and a bench and a candle
shrine along the side fences.

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:17.588
Step six, the residents.
Switch to the Skeletons kit,

00:03:17.588 --> 00:03:20.428
and drop a Skeleton
Warrior beside the path.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:25.715
Animated parts get an Animation menu in
the inspector. Search for Idle Combat,

00:03:25.715 --> 00:03:28.235
and pick it. Now he's ready for a fight.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:32.320
Use the square bracket keys
to turn him, 15° at a time.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:37.883
Add a mage casting a spell, a rogue, and
two minions. For the one at the open grave,

00:03:37.883 --> 00:03:42.758
choose Skeletons Awaken Floor Long, and
he will claw his way out of the ground,

00:03:42.758 --> 00:03:43.622
over and over.

00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:49.964
Step seven, dress the scene.
Back in the Halloween kit,

00:03:49.964 --> 00:03:53.954
put dead trees inside the fence,
and autumn pines outside it.

00:03:53.954 --> 00:03:56.963
Press plus or minus to
resize a selected part.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:05.042
For small clutter, place one
pumpkin, then use Scatter.

00:04:05.042 --> 00:04:09.175
It drops copies at random spots,
sizes and angles, with no overlaps.

00:04:09.175 --> 00:04:11.302
Do the same with bones and candles.

00:04:24.333 --> 00:04:30.489
Step eight, light. Press 3 to switch
the scene to night. Dark, isn't it?

00:04:30.489 --> 00:04:31.772
Let's fix that.

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:35.290
Stand a Post Lantern on
each side of the gate.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:39.903
The lantern is only a
model. To make it glow,

00:04:39.903 --> 00:04:43.589
click Point light at the top of the
parts list, and drop one next to it.

00:04:43.967 --> 00:04:47.428
In the inspector, raise it to
the lamp with the Y position.

00:04:47.428 --> 00:04:50.244
You can also change its
colour, power and range,

00:04:50.244 --> 00:04:53.294
and flame flicker makes it
dance like a real candle.

00:04:53.667 --> 00:04:56.942
Give every lantern, candle and
pumpkin its own small light.

00:04:56.942 --> 00:04:59.329
That's what makes a
night scene feel alive.

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:10.270
And that's the haunted
backyard. Hide the side panels,

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:12.847
and press Shift+F to
frame the whole scene.

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:17.409
Drag to orbit, right-drag
to pan, and scroll to zoom.

00:05:18.967 --> 00:05:21.288
When you're happy, click Export.

00:05:21.288 --> 00:05:27.091
You get a single GLB file with every
animation inside, ready for Blender, Unity,

00:05:27.091 --> 00:05:32.024
Godot or three.js. Or a zip, with
the project file and the licences.

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:37.748
Short on time? New project also has
Haunted backyard as a ready-made template.

00:05:37.748 --> 00:05:38.767
Have fun building!
